questions.question:
What does this print?

```js
console.log('1');
setTimeout(() => console.log('2'), 0);
Promise.resolve().then(() => console.log('3'));
queueMicrotask(() => console.log('4'));
console.log('5');
```

What does this print?

```js
for (var i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
  setTimeout(() => console.log(i));
}
```

What is wrong with this code?

```js
for (const id of ids) {
  const user = await fetchUser(id);
  users.push(user);
}
```

What does this print?

```js
async function f() {
  console.log('1');
  await null;
  console.log('2');
}
f();
console.log('3');
```

questions.explanation:
Debounce postpones the call until events stop for N ms — good for search-as-you-type. Throttle lets through at most one call per N ms — good for scroll and resize.

```js
function throttle(fn, ms) {
  let last = 0;
  let timer = null;
  return (...args) => {
    const now = Date.now();
    const rest = ms - (now - last);
    if (rest <= 0) {
      clearTimeout(timer);
      timer = null;
      last = now;
      fn(...args);
    } else if (!timer) {
      timer = setTimeout(() => {
        last = Date.now();
        timer = null;
        fn(...args);
      }, rest);
    }
  };
}
```

Without the trailing call the last event is lost — you will almost always be asked about that.
